{number: 137}
{title: Softly and Tenderly Jesus is Calling}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Softly and tenderly [Db] Jesus is [Ab] calling,
Calling for you and for [Eb7] me;
[Ab] See, on the portals He's [Db] waiting and [Ab] watching,
Watching for [Eb7] you and for [Ab] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb7] Come home, [Ab] come home,
[Bb7] Ye who are weary, [Eb7] come home;
[Ab] Earnestly, tenderly, [Db] Jesus is [Ab] calling,
Calling, O [Eb7] sinner, come [Ab] home!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Why should we tarry when [Db] Jesus is [Ab] pleading,
Pleading for you and for [Eb7] me?
[Ab] Why should we linger and [Db] heed not His [Ab] mercies,
Mercies for [Eb7] you and for [Ab] me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Time is now fleeting, the [Db] moments are [Ab] passing,
Passing from you and from [Eb7] me;
[Ab] Shadows are gathering, [Db] deathbeds are [Ab] coming,
Coming for [Eb7] you and for [Ab] me.
{end_of_verse}
